A||N||5||black-86-GT||Car idles to high||||8||
Z||000000||black-86-GT||04-10-2000||10:39 PM||||My car has been idleing high for about 3 weeks now. but about 1 week ago the S.E.S. light was coming on at idle then going away when I sped up. I checked it out and got a trouble code 35. Which is the IAC valve. I bought one and replaced it. but its still doing it. There shouldnt be any vacume leaks anywhere. but the front manifold is leaking pretty bad I dont know if that would make it idle high or not. also on a real hot day I get a code 32 For my egr valve. maybe that has something to do with it also. <P>If any of you guys can figure it out I sure could use the help I'ts really starting to annoy me. <P>Thanx||||reg||8
Z||000001||mwbackus||04-11-2000||06:09 AM||||A cracked EGR tube will cause high idle and sometimes even set a code 35. However, given that you have also observed the 32, I would bet that it is either a vacuum leak in the EGR solenoid or EGR solenoid supply line.<P>Mike B.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-11-2000||10:19 AM||||It sounds like  your EGR tube could be cracked. One more thing when you replace the IAC valve the car will run a high idle until you drive it over 40mph. this is when the ECM resets the IAC. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||black-86-GT||04-11-2000||07:45 PM||||Oh trust me the car definatly gets over 40MPH. the idle seems to be lowering but it still sticks around 1800 RPM's then slowly lowers. it seems to be good with the ac on. but today I checked the codes again and now im getting a code 24 speed sensor . I dont know whats going on||||reg||1
Z||000004||Boodoggin||04-12-2000||05:26 PM||||The same exact thing happened to my 86 GT.  I idled at 1700rpm and got trouble codes for the EGR and IAC. I replaced both of them...it did nothing.  I took it to my mechanic and he said I needed an entire new computer, but I didnt fall for it, it actually was just a cracked EGR tube, cost $90 to fix.  It seems like a lot of people have this problem for some reason.||||reg||1
Z||000005||David Gamache||04-12-2000||11:33 PM||||The EGR crossover tube sounds like a good bet. Remove it, cap one end and pour a little water in it and see if it leaks. the cracks are hard to find sometimes but this little test will let you know if there is a problem right away. If you are interested in a good used tube let me know and i will dig one up in the garage and let you have it for 25$ and whatever shipping would be. ||||reg||1
